cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "None"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141103" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}}.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{x}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 1 & =2\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true.* Therefore, the function $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{-1/2})}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{x}^{-1/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & =2\\sqrt{x} \\\\ -1 & =2x\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "560d0ead832ab0bfc59d6d138086f2ca1cd63c8fc973dec4ea5a09f6c4b83ea5" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2y}{x}-2,\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=2x$\n- $y={x}^{2}$\n- $y={x}^{3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot 2x}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}4-2 \\\\ 2 & =2.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{2},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot {x}^{2}}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}2x-2 \\\\ 0 & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *false*. Therefore, the function $y={x}^{2}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{3},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot {x}^{3}}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}2{x}^{2}-2 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ne -2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={x}^{3}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "560d0ead832ab0bfc59d6d138086f2ca1cd63c8fc973dec4ea5a09f6c4b83ea5" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79335" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79335" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf2cbefa57e10e55be069f2f4fb58b02bf911a3c2e6ea952d67aa496be33a158" "basis" 879 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980992/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79335" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and I